  "an10.54:13.1": "",
  "an10.54:13.2": "The word <i>sevitabba,</i> when used with material items, is usually translated as “to be partaken of.” When used with people, it is usually translated as “to be associated with.” However, here I have used the former rendering throughout to maintain the pattern of the original language, and also to point out the fact that when one associates with another person, one internalizes that person’s qualities and views.",
